            %p where
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ∇
                          %mrow
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                            %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla_{A,B}
                  is the
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Zilber+map"} Eilenberg-Zilber map
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Δ
                          %mrow
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                            %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_{A,B}
                  is the
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander-Whitney+map"} Alexander-Whitney map
            %p
          %p
            For unnormalized chain complexes, where we have a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Zilber+theorem"} Eilenberg-Zilber theorem
            (
            %a{:href => "#EilenbergZilber53"}> Eilenberg &amp; Zilber 1953
            ,
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#EilenbergMacLane54"} Eilenberg &amp; MacLane 1954, Thm. 2.1
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#MacLane75"} MacLane 1975, VIII 8
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Dold95"} Dold 1995, VI 12.1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+retraction"} deformation retraction
            for normalized chain complexes is
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#EilenbergMacLane54"} Eilenberg &amp; MacLane 1954, Thm. 2.1a
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#May67"} May 1967, Cor. 29.10
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#MacLane75"} MacLane 1975, VIII Cor. 8.9
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+operator"} homotopy operator
            is given in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#GonzalezDiazReal99"} Gonzalez-Diaz &amp; Real 1999, p. 7
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %strong Alexander-Whitney map
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Zilber+map"} Eilenberg-Zilber map
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Zilber+theorem"} Eilenberg-Zilber theorem
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#EilenbergZilber53
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Samuel+Eilenberg"}> Samuel Eilenberg
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joseph+Zilber"} Joseph Zilber
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On Products of Complexes
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/2372629"} jstor:2372629
            %li#EilenbergMacLane54
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Samuel+Eilenberg"}> Samuel Eilenberg
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saunders+MacLane"} Saunders MacLane
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    On the Groups
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi H
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Π
                            %mo ,
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H(\Pi,n)
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/1969702"} jstor:1969702
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2307/2372629"} doi:10.2307/2372629
          %p
            using the definition of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Zilber+map"} Eilenberg-Zilber map
            in:
          %ul
            %li#EilenbergMacLane53
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Samuel+Eilenberg"}> Samuel Eilenberg
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saunders+MacLane"} Saunders MacLane
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  On the groups
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Π
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H(\Pi,n)
              %em
                , Ann. of Math. (2) 58, (1953), 55–106. (
                %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/1969820"}> jstor:1969820
                )
          %p Review and further discussion:
          %ul
            %li#May67
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"}> Peter May
                , Section 29 of:
                %em Simplicial objects in algebraic topology
                , Chicago Lectures in Mathematics, University of Chicago Press 1967 (
                %a{:href => "https://press.uchicago.edu/ucp/books/book/chicago/S/bo5956688.html"}> ISBN:9780226511818
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/BOOKS/Simp.djvu"} djvu
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/May_SimplicialObjectsInAlgebraicTopology.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#MacLane75
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saunders+Mac+Lane"}> Saunders Mac Lane
                ,
                %em Homology
                (1975) reprinted as Classics in Mathematics. Springer-Verlag, Berlin, 1995. x+422 pp. ISBN 3-540-58662-8 (
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-642-62029-4"}> doi:10.1007/978-3-642-62029-4
                )
            %li#Dold95
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Albrecht+Dold"}> Albrecht Dold
                , Section VI 12.1 in
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lectures on Algebraic Topology
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.springer.com/gp/book/9783540586609"} doi:10.1007/978-3-642-67821-9
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/bfm%3A978-3-642-67821-9%2F1.pdf"} pdf
            %li#GonzalezDiazReal99
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rocio+Gonzalez-Diaz"}> Rocio Gonzalez-Diaz
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pedro+Real"} Pedro Real
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A Combinatorial Method for Computing Steenrod Squares
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0110308"} arXiv:math/0110308
